-- chem/fermi.cub — operators of fermions as terms with a normal form. A letter is a creator or an annihilator of a
-- mode; a word is a product of letters; an operator is a list of (word, rational). The rules are the three of
-- exclusion: a_p a†_q = δ_pq − a†_q a_p, two creators (two annihilators) exchange with a sign, and the square of a
-- letter is zero. The normal form has creators first, then annihilators, each by increasing mode; `fa-put` moves one
-- letter into a normal word by those rules, and a product is letters put in one at a time. Two operators are equal
-- exactly when their normal forms agree (`fa-eq`): an operator identity (a certificate that H − λ is a sum of
-- squares B†B is one) is decided by this, with no matrix built and for every number of particles at once.
import "algebra.cub"

